<title>BELGIUM: EU ends anti-dumping work on Japanese EPROMs.</title>
<headline>EU ends anti-dumping work on Japanese EPROMs.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has ended anti-dumping investigations into Japanese imports of EPROM microelectronic circuitry, allow currently suspended measures to lapse, said the EU Official Journal on Thursday.</p>
<p>European Union dumping measures against Japanese EPROMs, a term which stands for Erasable Programmable Read Only Memories, have been suspended since June 1995.</p>
<p>The Commission rejected EU industry claims that certain sectors of the EPROM market remained prone to price crashes and found that Japanese imports did not cause &quot;injury&quot; to EU-origin sales during the investigation period.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
